  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Guard",
      "items": [
        "Asks before a costly cold send, once per cold episode: Send anyway, or Don't send (hold, 0 AI credits)",
        "No answer in 5 minutes holds the send. A host that cannot ask gets the old refuse-once message",
        "Shell escapes (!) and a fixed list of local commands (/help, /clear, /model, ...) are never guarded; /compact and skill commands are guarded like a prompt",
        "The local-command list is unverified on a real host. A running turn only gets the price note",
        "A cold send on a model with no known price warns once per cold episode, then sends",
        "refusals/<sha256 of the session id>.json lets the next send, even from a new process, through"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Clock",
      "items": [
        "TTL, expiry and prices come from assistant.usage; nothing is guessed",
        "assistant.usage is not replayed on resume, so events.jsonl seeds the clock",
        "Heads-up leads by the smaller of the setting and a fifth of the TTL, never mid-turn, and stays quiet while a keep-warm ping is planned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Keep-warm",
      "items": [
        "Off until turned on. keepwarm on means 3 hours after your last real message; the most is 12 hours",
        "A ping fires 20% of the cache lifetime before expiry, between 30 s and 6 min, and pings are never closer than 60 s",
        "It stops by itself on its budget ($0.50 by default, 0 to 5), on payback, on its daily limit ($2 by default, 0.10 to 20), on a cold or unmeasured reply, or on a failed send",
        "attribution.mjs decides whether a usage record is the ping's or yours. With no user.message from the host, the first record during a ping goes to the ping",
        "One process per session pings. The lock holder refreshes the lock every 10 min, and a lock silent for 30 min is taken over even if its pid is alive",
        "Window, lock and ledger are 0600 files in a 0700 keepwarm/ directory. The ledger compacts under the lock once it passes 64 KiB"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "VS Code, measured 11-12 Oct 2026",
      "items": [
        "Extension loads only with chat.canvases.enabled, from a project install (.github/extensions)",
        "Cards, help and settings show as a question with OK; the heads-up reaches only VS Code's log",
        "Cold-send warnings are sent at error level in VS Code so the chat shows them (set in the code, not re-measured there)",
        "Sessions keep usage checkpoints only, so the report counts them as totals"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Limits",
      "items": [
        "Reported expiry is an upper bound: Luna was served cold at 29 of 30 minutes",
        "/cache-clock works typed in full in VS Code but is not in its / menu",
        "Keep-warm pings have not been run against a real host: the ping, its attribution and its cost reading are unverified there",
        "Each ping is a model turn that costs money. It sends billable: false where the host has the rpc send, and whether the host honours that is unverified",
        "In copilot -p the same guard rule applies (no reliable -p signal), so a local-command name typed there may reach the model cold, unguarded; unverified"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
